  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much down payment do I need in Torrance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Down payment depends on loan type and price. Many Torrance buyers use conventional financing with as little as 3 to 5 percent down when they qualify, or FHA with 3.5 percent on eligible properties. Higher-priced homes in parts of 90503 or 90505 may use jumbo financing where lenders often expect more equity, though options vary. Closing costs are separate from your down payment. I map cash to close before you write an offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What credit score is needed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Conventional financing often starts around 620 for basic eligibility, with stronger pricing as scores rise. FHA may work with scores of 580 or higher for 3.5 percent down on qualifying purchases. Jumbo loans for premium South Bay neighborhoods frequently look for 700 or higher. Your full file, not one number, decides what is realistic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does pre-approval take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If you send documents promptly, many buyers receive a written pre-approval within a few business days after we speak. Same-day direction is possible when timing is tight; the priority is accuracy. For a checklist of what to gather, read my article on how to get pre-approved for a mortgage."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I buy with FHA in Torrance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when the property qualifies. FHA is on the table for many buyers in pockets such as North Torrance when the home and any condo project meet HUD and lender guidelines. It is not automatic for every listing; project approval and property condition matter. I check FHA viability for the specific address early so you do not waste time on a mismatch."}}]}</script>
