          <h2 id="pre-heading">Start with a pre-approval</h2>
          <p>Pre-approval is the bridge between “I want to live in Torrance” and “here is my offer.” It tells you what payment and cash-to-close look like on paper, and it gives your agent a number the listing side can trust.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">Short call.</strong> Timeline, price range, and whether this is a first purchase or a move-up within the South Bay.</li>
            <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">Documents.</strong> Pay stubs, W-2s or tax returns, bank statements — only what your file needs, spelled out up front.</li>
            <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">Credit &amp; debt review.</strong> We address surprises early instead of in escrow.</li>
            <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">Program match.</strong> Align <a href="https://www.rudycorona.com/services/conventional/">conventional</a> or <a href="https://www.rudycorona.com/services/fha/">FHA</a> (or other products) with the actual homes you are targeting.</li>
            <li><strong style="color:var(--text);">Letter in hand.</strong> A limit grounded in real questions — plus my guide on <a href="https://www.rudycorona.com/blog/how-to-get-pre-approved-mortgage/">how to get pre-approved for a mortgage</a> so you know what the letter means.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>When you are ready, use the <a href="https://www.rudycorona.com/contact/">contact page</a> or call <strong>(310) 594-5362</strong>.</p>
